                      <history>
                         <origin>
                           <origDate notBefore="1700" notAfter="1799">18th century.</origDate>
                             King ʾIyāsu mentioned in the colophon could be possibly <persName ref="PRS5616IyasuI">ʾIyāsu I</persName> 
                             (reigned <date>1682–1706</date>) or <persName ref="PRS5616IyasuI"> ʾIyāsu II</persName> 
                             (reigned <date>1730–1755</date>) ca. 1698 or ca. 1771.
                             There is a hint to the mileau of <persName ref="PRS11207Ewostateans">ʾEwosṭāteans</persName>
                             as the context of the creation of the work (and the manuscript?). 
                             </origin>
                          
